<% noise = run["noise"] || {} -%>
<div class="page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Noise</p>
  <h1>Noise filtered</h1>
  <p>Control A and control A′ run the same Rails version on the same traffic. Anything that differs between them is noise (random tokens, unfrozen time). Differences between control A and candidate B at those paths are not reported.</p>
</div>
<section class="card" aria-label="Noise counts">
  <ul class="tiles stats">
    <li class="tile stat"><span class="stat-value"><%= noise["a_vs_a_prime_differences"].to_i %></span> <span class="stat-label">differences between control A and control A′ (noise observed)</span></li>
    <li class="tile stat"><span class="stat-value"><%= noise["a_vs_b_differences"].to_i %></span> <span class="stat-label">differences between control A and candidate B</span></li>
    <li class="tile stat"><span class="stat-value"><%= noise["suppressed"].to_i %></span> <span class="stat-label">of those suppressed as noise</span></li>
  </ul>
</section>
<% masked = noise["masked_paths"] || {} -%>
<section class="card<%= " table-card" unless masked.empty? %>" aria-labelledby="masked-heading">
  <div class="card-head"><h2 id="masked-heading">Masked paths by route</h2></div>
<% if masked.empty? -%>
  <p>No paths were masked: control A and control A′ produced identical normalized traces.</p>
<% else -%>
  <p class="pad-x">A real upgrade difference at one of these paths would also be hidden; check them if a route matters to you (RISKS R11).</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Route</th><th scope="col">Masked paths</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
<% masked.each do |route, paths| -%>
      <tr><td><code><%= h(route) %></code></td><td><ul class="plain"><% paths.each do |p| %><li><code><%= h(p) %></code></li><% end %></ul></td></tr>
<% end -%>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end -%>
</section>
